  "reputation": {
    "summary": "NwAvGuy measured it for the O2 and chose it for the gain stage: quieter than NE5532, LM4562 and OPA2134 at lower current, for under a dollar. Soomal found it in E-MU interfaces, Chinese sound cards and many CD players, calling it very low noise, high resolution, neutral. Japanese swappers know it as the classic quiet JRC dual.",
    "sonic_descriptors": [
      "very low noise (噪声很小)",
      "high resolution (解析力高)",
      "neutral, plain (中性平白)",
      "relaxed, ample bass",
      "dense, mellow (unverified)"
    ],
    "typical_uses": [
      "O2 (Objective2) and SmartStand headphone amp gain stages",
      "E-MU 0202/0204/0404/1212m; Musiland X-Sword II, ooAoo SQ710 II/SQ717a",
      "Japanese CD, AV (Yamaha YSP-600) and car (Pioneer KEX-M8406ZT) units",
      "MM phono preamps (FX-Audio BOX-01/BOX-02)",
      "Roland VG-99/GK-3 inputs; ICON PX-T6A active monitors"
    ],
    "caveats": [
      "Capacitive loads can oscillate: add about 50 Ω in series (vendor). One note.com user reports NJM2068D oscillating in a preamp.",
      "Needs ±4 V (8 V) minimum: unsuitable for 5 V or USB-powered designs.",
      "'27 MHz' is GB at 10 kHz; unity-gain frequency is only 5.5 MHz.",
      "No nV/√Hz or current-noise spec; bias current up to 1 µA. Keep source and feedback impedances low.",
      "Not a headphone driver: output current unspecified, loads ≥2 kΩ. O2 pairs it with NJM4556A."
    ],
    "sources": [
